.TH CASE_LOWERC 3
.SH NAME
case_lowerc \- convert a character to lowercase
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <case.h>
.PP
.BI "int case_lowerc(int " c ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B case_lowerc
converts an uppercase ASCII character to its lowercase equivalent.
.PP
If the character
.I c
is an uppercase letter ('A'-'Z'), it is converted to the corresponding lowercase letter ('a'-'z'). All other characters are returned unchanged. This function operates on ASCII values and does not account for locale-specific character sets.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the lowercase version of the input character, or the input character itself if it is not an uppercase letter.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR case_upperc (3),
.BR byte_lower (3)